@startuml
!include _libcpg-theme.iuml
title Mode A / Mode B build equivalence invariant (test_build_from_tree_matches_build)
start
:same source + Language::Rust;
fork
  :Mode A
build(source, Language::Rust)
[needs feature lang-rust —
parses internally via ParserRegistry];<<#DBE4FF>>
fork again
  :Mode B
tree_sitter::Parser.parse(source)
-> build_from_tree(&tree, source, Language::Rust)
[feature-free — caller owns the tree];<<#DBE4FF>>
end fork
:assert node_count and edge_count identical
(and language() equal);<<#C3FAE8>>
stop
note right
  Mode A delegates its post-parse pipeline to
  Mode B, so the two graphs are identical in shape.
  Mode B skips the <latex>max\_file\_size</latex> check —
  the caller already owns the parse tree.
end note
legend right
  |= colour |= role |
  |<#DBE4FF>| parse + AST/CFG/DFG build |
  |<#C3FAE8>| equivalence assertion |
endlegend
@enduml
